# Stack contracts

## While architecture unlocked
If `.cursor/brain/DECISIONS.md` architecture is not human-locked, do not invent
a stack here. A **proposal** may already live in DECISIONS §Architecture
(native C++ peer desktop). Follow that proposal only after the human locks it;
until then, no feature scaffolding of capture/protocol/UI.

## After architecture lock
Follow the locked Client / API / Data / Auth / Sync choices in DECISIONS.md.
Do not silently diverge in code without updating DECISIONS.

## Persistence
- Never silently fall back from real persistence (DB/files) to in-memory fakes
  on production paths.
- Empty queries → empty results; infra failures → explicit errors (not fake data).

## Disabled / deferred features
- Status or upgrade UI only — **no invented business CRUD** for features that
  are out of scope, unpaid, or not yet `build-ready`.

## Module ownership
- Respect CODEMAP and DECISIONS §Boundaries when they exist.
- Prefer one module directory → one PR when possible.

## Growing rules
When `frontend/`, `backend/`, or equivalent folders exist, add thin glob-scoped
`.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files that **point at** brain DECISIONS/CODEMAP — do not
paste another product’s stack rules verbatim.
